  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1106 AM CDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nRecent satellite obs show an advancing outflow boundary beginning\nto stall across far NE AR, MO bootheel and NW TN. Behind the\nboundary NE winds and slightly cooler, but more humid conditions\nprovide no real relief from summer heat. A transient shower could\nform along or behind this boundary later this afternoon, but\nwidespread coverage or rainfall is expected. \n\nThe persistent ridge across Central CONUS will continue ushering\nin warmer temps over the weekend. Combined with southerly flow\ndrawing more moisture into the area swampy conditions will return\nthrough the weekend. A Heat Advisory is in effect in the MS River\nDelta for Friday afternoon, and further heat products into the\nweekend and next week will be on the table. \n\nRain chances over the weekend could help limit some of the heat.\nAn upper level trough in phase with a weak short wave should help\ndrive PoPs as it gets squeezed between two high pressures systems\nsieging the FA. After this weak system and PoPs look to be limited\nto any afternoon summer-time popups.",
